From: Androlinzberg maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] icu jni: initialize the status passed to Locale::forLanguageTag

ScopedIcuLocale passes an uninitialized UErrorCode to forLanguageTag, which
returns early on a failure code it finds already set. On this host the stack
slot holds a nonzero value, so every locale is bogus and CaseMapperNative
returns null: String.toLowerCase of any text with a surrogate pair, or under
a Turkic locale, becomes null. The AOSP source relies on the slot being zero.
--- a/android_icu4j/libcore_bridge/src/native/ScopedIcuLocale.h
+++ b/android_icu4j/libcore_bridge/src/native/ScopedIcuLocale.h
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@
       return;
     }
 
-    UErrorCode err;
+    UErrorCode err = U_ZERO_ERROR;
     icu::Locale locale = icu::Locale::forLanguageTag(languageTag.c_str(), err);
     if (U_FAILURE(err)) {
       return;
